WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
The Lake District: England's
largest national park,

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.910
and a World Heritage Site since 2017.

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.730
The 2021 census counted 38,993 residents.

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:18.330
In 2025, it drew 17.45 million tourists.

5
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:27.390
In 2025, 7,035 of its 23,839 homes
were second homes or holiday lets.

6
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.600
That's 29.5 per cent.

7
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.510
14.8 per cent were holiday lets.

8
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.130
14.6 per cent were second homes.

9
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.970
So who is the park for?

10
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.070
Local families?

11
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.410
Farmers?

12
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:40.790
Visitors?

13
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.430
Or the whole nation?

14
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.870
In this mission, you'll weigh
changes in the park's economy,

15
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.670
housing, population and environment.

16
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.450
Then you'll test the plans
meant to balance farmers,

17
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.570
residents and visitors.

18
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.310
Your mission: decide who
the Lake District is for,

19
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.170
and how you would judge
whether it is working.
